What are your responsibilities?
• Repairing and maintaining all equipment and tools
• Building preventive maintenance
• Plumbing, electrical and ventilation works
• Ensuring the hotel meets it's health and safety requirements What makes you the perfect fit?To be eligible for this position:
• You can speak English as well as understand basic Dutch;
• You have previous experience in mechanics, plumbing and air-conditioning;
• You have previous hotel maintenance experience;
• You are willing to work mornings, evenings and weekends. What do you get in return?The Amsterdam Marriott Hotel is part of Marriott International and offers a competitive salary & a wide package of benefits. Each year you will have a performance appraisal and depending on your performance you will get a salary increase. Furthermore we offer:
• Special discounted rates for 10.000+ Marriott hotels worldwide for you, your family and friends;
• A special discount of 50% in a selection of fine bars and restaurants in 5 star hotel properties in Amsterdam;
• Monthly gross salary with a range from €2600 to €2725,03
• Personal coaching & training to support you in your day-to-day job;
• Career possibilities within Marriott Internat

You start each workday with a friendly chat with your colleagues, making sure everyone is focused and ready to get to work. As a Warehouse Operator, you and your team are responsible for ensuring the warehouse operates efficiently. As a Warehouse Operator, you ensure the warehouse runs smoothly by picking orders with a handheld scanner, packing and labelling products, transporting pallets with an Electric Pallet Truck (EPT), wrapping pallets,  checking orders for accuracy, preparing shipments, and maintaining a clean and safe working environment. You are also happy to support other departments whenever needed, because teamwork is at the heart of DSV.

This is what we ask from you:

- You are at least 18 years old and have a VMBO level of education or equivalent working and thinking level;
- You have a good command of the English language;
- You are willing to work in two shifts (06.00-15.00 / 15.00-00.00); 
- You are not allowed to wear metal jewelry, piercings, shoes, belts, phones, or smartwatches;
- You live within commuting distance of Moerdijk and have your own transportation;

As an E&I Maintenance Technician, you will be responsible for maintaining, installing, and troubleshooting electrical and instrumentation systems within industrial plants. You will work with control systems, sensors, measuring equipment, and electrical installations to keep industrial processes running smoothly.

Your responsibilities include:

- Installing and connecting instrumentation and electrical systems;
- Testing, calibrating, and commissioning measuring instruments;
- Performing preventive and corrective maintenance activities;
- Troubleshooting faults in electrical and control systems;
- Ensuring all work complies with safety standards and regulations, including ATEX guidelines.
- You will work independently as well as together with colleagues on industrial projects and maintenance operations.

- MBO level 3 or 4 in Electrical Engineering, Instrumentation, Mechatronics, or similar;
- Experience with E&I systems in industrial environments;
- Knowledge of NEN 3140 and preferably ATEX;
- Valid VCA certificate or willingness to obtain one;
- Driving license B;
- Accurate, proactive, and solution-oriented mindset;
- Good communication skills in Dutch or English.
